.TH PHPFPM-AUTO-OPTIMIZE 8 "August 2026" "phpfpm-auto-optimize 0.5.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
phpfpm-auto-optimize \- calculate and safely apply PHP-FPM pool capacity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B phpfpm-auto-optimize
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inventories PHP-FPM pools, estimates worker memory, considers recent saturation
warnings, and recommends a globally memory-bounded configuration. The default
mode is read-only. Applying writes a late-loading override, validates it, and
transactionally reloads affected services.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --apply
Install, validate, and activate recommendations. Requires root.
.TP
.B --check
Perform a dry run and exit 2 when changes are recommended.
.TP
.B --json
Emit versioned machine-readable dry-run output.
.TP
.BI --config " PATH"
Read policy defaults from a regular configuration file.
.TP
.BI --pool-dir " PATH"
Manage a pool directory. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI --instance " SPEC"
Map DIR|BINARY|MASTER_CONFIG[|SERVICE] for validation and activation.
.TP
.BI --monitor-seconds " N"
Sample PHP-FPM workers and system memory for N seconds before recommending.
.TP
.BI --sample-interval " N"
Set monitoring frequency in seconds, from 1 through 60.
.TP
.BI --log-file " [DIR=]PATH"
Read a PHP-FPM error log, optionally binding it to a pool directory.
.TP
.B --list-backups
List backup run identifiers.
.TP
.BI --restore " ID|PATH"
Restore a manifested backup. Currently requires
.BR --no-reload .
.TP
.B --no-reload
Install or restore files without service activation.
.TP
.B --help
Display the complete option list and defaults.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/phpfpm-auto-optimize.conf
is the default policy file.
.I /var/backups/phpfpm-auto-optimize
contains run manifests and prior generated overrides.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success, 1 indicates an error, and 2 means
.B --check
found recommended changes.
.SH SECURITY
Privileged policy files must be root-owned and not group/world writable. Review
a dry run before applying. See SECURITY.md in the source distribution.
